  "details": "This is both a request and genuinely a question about VRC audio as well.\n\nI use a non-standardized audio input of VRC for content creation and streaming, just a XLR lav mic. I also perform music in VRC. It seems like there is no true open mic mode at least for me. When I set gates off and let the pure signal from my mic come though there is a soft gate I can hear cutting the signal out. I can't tell if this is something built into the game from Unity or Steam spatial audio stuff or maybe a internet packet loss issue or something from me. Having a pure decay is pretty important for musicians and performers. \n\nIf there is something I am missing, please let me know. Discord output seems fine, and they have a reduced processing mode called Studio Mode which I use.\n\nThanks!",
